 "answer": "**It depends on where you are in Jakarta.** As of **11:00 p.m. Saturday, October 17, Jakarta time**, the city’s air-quality monitor showed *moderate* pollution in Pasar Minggu (ISPU 60), where outdoor activity was generally considered okay. But a monitor in Tanjung Priok showed *unhealthy* pollution (ISPU 169), where the city advises limiting prolonged or strenuous outdoor activity. Check the reading nearest your route before exercising. ([udara.jakarta.go.id](https://udara.jakarta.go.id/))\n\nIf your nearby reading is moderate, an easy workout is reasonable; if it’s unhealthy, **move a hard workout indoors**. For daytime exercise, heat is another concern: today’s forecast high was **36°C (96°F)**, with a warning about dehydration and heatstroke during extended time outside. ([udara.jakarta.go.id](https://udara.jakarta.go.id/))",
